note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note Library admission (developer bars D2, D6): which PCI GPU CUDA++ may open, decided before nvrm_open opens any /dev/nvidia node.
note The C side (src/omega_gpu_chip.c) only reads /sys/bus/pci/devices, compares the CUDAPP_GPU_BDF string and formats the sentence.
note PCI ids: vendor NVIDIA 0x10de=4318. GB10 0x2e12=11794 runs sm_121 (the chip row of src/omega_gpu_chip.c).
note Prepared Ampere rows, device tests NOT_RUN (docs/PORT-AMPERE.md, tests/ampere/README.md): GA102 0x2204=8708, GA104 0x2486=9350, 0x2489=9353, sm_86.
note Class word: PCI base class 0x03 (display or 3D controller) is class shr 16.
fn chip_target vendor ulong device ulong cls ulong to ulong
if or ne vendor 4318 ne shr cls 16 3
ret 0
end
if eq device 11794
ret 121
end
if or eq device 8708 or eq device 9350 eq device 9353
ret 86
end
ret 0
end
note Bad input: every output word is cleared, then status 4.
fn chip_bad o edit ulong 4 to ulong
for k ulong 4
put o k 0
end
put o 0 4
ret 4
end
note d[4i..4i+3] = vendor, device, class, bdf match (0 or 1) for i below n, n at most 16. want=1 when CUDAPP_GPU_BDF is set.
note Without want every NVIDIA display GPU must be a target (the driver picks the first card). With want only the matched one counts.
note o[0] status: 0 admitted, 1 no NVIDIA display GPU, 2 the BDF matches no NVIDIA display GPU, 3 not a CUDA++ target, 4 bad input.
note o[1] entry index, o[2] target sm (0 unless admitted), o[3] PCI device id. Returns o[0].
fn chip_admit d view ulong 64 n ulong want ulong o edit ulong 4 to ulong
for k ulong 4
put o k 0
end
if or gt n 16 gt want 1
ret chip_bad o
end
seen = ulong 0
for i ulong 16
if ge i n
break
end
b = mul i 4
v = get d b
dev = get d add b 1
cls = get d add b 2
hit = get d add b 3
if gt hit 1
ret chip_bad o
end
if and eq v 4318 eq shr cls 16 3
if or eq want 0 eq hit 1
seen = add seen 1
if and eq want 1 gt seen 1
ret chip_bad o
end
t = chip_target v dev cls
if eq t 0
put o 0 3
put o 1 i
put o 2 0
put o 3 dev
ret 3
end
if eq seen 1
put o 1 i
put o 2 t
put o 3 dev
end
end
end
end
if eq seen 0
if eq want 1
put o 0 2
ret 2
end
put o 0 1
ret 1
end
ret 0
end
